Always publish simulator state, even while the Betaflight link is down.

SendState() was gated on betaflightOnline, which is only set by receiving a
motor packet. Betaflight SITL is strictly reactive: measured in isolation it
emits exactly one unprompted motor packet at startup and thereafter one packet
per FDM packet received. So once the plugin misses connectionTimeoutMaxCount
motor packets it stops sending state, SITL stops responding, and neither side
can restart the other -- the link deadlocks permanently.

Publishing state unconditionally costs one UDP datagram per step when nothing
is listening and lets a dropped link recover on its own. Motor forces stay
gated so stale commands are not applied while offline.

diff --git a/plugins/BetaflightPlugin.cc b/plugins/BetaflightPlugin.cc
index 2725828..039c509 100644
--- a/plugins/BetaflightPlugin.cc
+++ b/plugins/BetaflightPlugin.cc
@@ -580,12 +580,15 @@ void BetaflightPluginPrivate::OnUpdate(EntityComponentManager &_ecm,
   if (_simTime > this->lastControllerUpdateTime)
   {
     this->ReceiveMotorCommand();
+    auto dt = std::chrono::duration<double>(
+        _simTime - this->lastControllerUpdateTime).count();
     if (this->betaflightOnline)
     {
-      auto dt = std::chrono::duration<double>(_simTime - this->lastControllerUpdateTime).count();
       this->ApplyMotorForces(dt, _ecm);
-      this->SendState(_ecm);
     }
+    // SITL only emits a motor packet in response to state, so gating this
+    // makes a dropped link unrecoverable.
+    this->SendState(_ecm);
   }
 
   this->lastControllerUpdateTime = _simTime;
